{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967370-is-it-time-to-relax-our-airport-security","id":967370,"title":"Is it time to relax our airport security?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-11T09:48:11-07:00","id":967370,"title":"Is it time to relax our airport security?","content":"Seems an appropriate day to bring this up...<br /> <br /> This has been something bugging me for awhile now, but I always hesitate to bring it up because it seems such a hot-button topic. Still, that <a href=\"http://ktla.com/2016/08/28/lax-closed-to-incoming-traffic-due-to-police-activity-airport-police/\" target=\"_blank\">recent incident where JFK airport was closed because people panicked when they heard loud noises they mistook for gunshots</a> (and a Zorro cosplayer arrested for having a plastic sword) really brought it home. Has our airport security gone too far?<br /> <br /> I kind of liken this nation of America to a person who never had any direct experience of crime or violence, but was suddenly robbed one day in a home invasion, during which he was beaten or even shot...as he recovered, he naturally sought to protect himself in the future, placing multiple locks on his doors, installing elaborate security devices, and even patting down any and all visitors to his place. But now, fifteen years later, his friends might want to ask him if this lifestyle of his is frankly overreacting. After all, the police caught the guy who broke in and he was executed on Death Row a few years back. Of course, that guy had friends, and they may also wish our guy harm, but nothing's happened in all that time since...Isn't it about time he stopped being so paranoid?<br /> <br /> Ok, I'm gonna abandon this analogy before it gets even more elaborate! The point is, does the long, inconvenient process of getting through an airport really serve us, or is it a placebo for our nation psychosocial trauma, put in place by politicians just to show that they take this seriously? Even many of the people who initially clamored for the government to &quot;do something&quot; have largely long since realized that it's more trouble than its worth, once they themselves are greatly inconvenienced by it...After years of unlocking ten locks just to get in and out of the house, I think we're slowly, finally coming to the embarrassing conclusion that, just maybe, we've overreacted a bit.<br /> <br /> But no one can speak up and say anything. Because, if you do, you run the risk of seeming &quot;unAmerican&quot; or &quot;soft on Terrorism&quot;, which is why no politician is EVER likely to advocate loosening airport security for improved transport of the people, it would be political suicide as their political enemies publicly crucified them for it. *Maybe* if enough civilian groups started a movement to relax security measures, showing such a public desire to be popular enough, however...<br /> <br /> Of course, the real question comes back around to <i>should</i> we? After all, terrorists DO still exist and do still mean us harm. Are they likely to take advantage of lessened air security again? The methodology of terrorist attacks is to attack by surprise where one least expects it, and *everyone* is watching the skies now, suggests it is unlikely...but it's certainly not impossible. And, of course, no one wants to be the one who advocated lessened security right before the next attack! <br /> <br /> So...are we just stuck with this state of affairs? Locked in to this current way of doing things, until either our grandchildren just say &quot;this is bullshit!&quot; and loosen things up (unlikely, as that will be the system they are born into and therefore, the norm for them) or we somehow wipe out the specter of terrorist once and for all (even more unlikely, sadly)? Or is there some more effective, saner way to both deal with securing our skies AND dealing with our collective trauma?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:06:59-07:00","id":967382,"title":"","content":"I don't think it serves us as much as the airports and airplane companies, who presumably lose more money over hijackings or crashes and might even face legal repercussions if they allow certain people on board without checking thoroughly.<br /> <br /> Without being able to link to any instances offhand, I know there have been more than a few incidents where someone got on board a plane that shouldn't have or with something they couldn't have gotten on with. And I can't think of any time TSA actually managed to stop anyone from doing anything but get on their assigned flight in peace. Every incident I hear about them involves them harassing women, children or the handicapped, or abusing their authority and ability and outright engaging in criminal acts.<br /> <br /> Really don't see things changing anytime soon, however. Especially with the turmoil Daesh and other hate groups are bringing to the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T10:10:04-07:00","id":967383,"title":"","content":"Decrease airport security? Absolutely not! <br /> <br /> Decrease the pointless and proven ineffectual airport security theater? It's past due.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:18:29-07:00","id":967492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967370-is-it-time-to-relax-our-airport-security?p=967382#post967382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it serves us as much as the airports and airplane companies, who presumably lose more money over hijackings or crashes and might even face legal repercussions if they allow certain people on board without checking thoroughly.<br /> <br /> Without being able to link to any instances offhand, I know there have been more than a few incidents where someone got on board a plane that shouldn't have or with something they couldn't have gotten on with. And I can't think of any time TSA actually managed to stop anyone from doing anything but get on their assigned flight in peace. Every incident I hear about them involves them harassing women, children or the handicapped, or abusing their authority and ability and outright engaging in criminal acts.<br /> <br /> Really don't see things changing anytime soon, however. Especially with the turmoil Daesh and other hate groups are bringing to the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heck, the # of times CNN or 20.20 have done shows showing how easy it WAS to get by TSA with stuff, makes me wonder why we don't disband it, and make each airport/airline have their OWN security..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T13:56:40-07:00","id":967516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/967370-is-it-time-to-relax-our-airport-security?p=967383#post967383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Decrease airport security? Absolutely not!<br /> <br /> Decrease the pointless and proven ineffectual airport security theater? It's past due.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>QFT. I would prefer a tighter but actually effective security apparatus like Israel has to what we have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T14:49:41-07:00","id":967534,"title":"","content":"Israel has impeccable airport security that happens to look absolutely nothing like American airport security. We don't need to cut back so much as actually do literally anything more effective than the current situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T17:56:25-07:00","id":967631,"title":"","content":"A friend of mine was there for that, and he complained to me about how pure apeshit chaotic it was, and how nobody knew what to do and nobody was helping.<br /> <br /> I could do without being racially profiled by a security body that's ineffectual. That'd be really nice. I think individual airports handling security is a great way to create a wildly inconsistent level of security that would cause more problems than it would solve.<br /> <br /> What exactly does Israel do?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T20:11:30-07:00","id":967700,"title":"","content":"Israeli airport security focuses on a few things:<br /> <br /> 1) All random screenings are in fact random, and are done to vehicles approaching the airport (this avoids profiling because it's just based on picking vehicles as they come in before they can see who's in them), rather than in some stupid waiting room where you could blow up the lines of people waiting to get scanned if you're about to get caught.<br /> <br /> 2) Minimize or eliminate gathering places/bottlenecks that exist before security is done with you. One of the reasons the TSA methods are so dumb is that they only care about if you get on the plane with something, and completely ignore that killing a terminal full of people is still devastating terrorism. As noted, having huge bottleneck lines at check-in, or at security check points, makes those places targets for desperate terrorists fearing they can't get to the plane.<br /> <br /> 3) Security checkpoints are located in reinforced concrete hallways (though generally disguised) to minimize the ability for mass causalities even further.<br /> <br /> 4) Security checkpoints exist at the exits of airports as well as entrances to avoid baggage claims becoming targets as well.<br /> <br /> 5) And most important? Security officers are highly trained and generally recruited from law enforcement backgrounds rather than being minimally trained people running a checklist. They're trained to engage you in conversation specifically to look for cues or tells that you're up to something. Ideally, you never even know you were being seriously screened because it should feel like a pleasant small chat while they check your papers and scan your bags so you feel completely comfortable and open.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T22:09:31-07:00","id":967769,"title":"","content":"In addition to the above, from what I've seen the interviews given at screenings are less about &quot;DO YOU HAVE A BOMB AND ARE YOU GOING TO BLOW UP THIS PLANE? NO? ENJOY YOUR FLIGHT, CITIZEN,&quot; and more about trying to see if the person being interviewed actually has a halfway consistent story about who they are, where they're going, and what they want to do there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T01:09:15-07:00","id":967820,"title":"","content":"Plus they profile.. We scan 4 yr olds, 90 yr olds, people in wheel chairs etc, all so we DON'T profile so as to not offend anyone... which to be is total BS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-12T11:28:04-07:00","id":968041,"title":"","content":"While they do profile, they have all sorts of groups they pay attention to besides what most people think.<br /> <br /> For example, people that are on charity paid trips to Israel (something a few Jewish and Christian groups do to allow people to see the Holy Land), are often profiled because in the past they've been used in drug smuggling operations,and they're looking for dupes/mules that are being used to carry drugs into the country.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T00:39:26-07:00","id":971809,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/blog/7-reasons-tsa-sucks-a-security-experts-perspective/\" target=\"_blank\">This Cracked article</a> is relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}